module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.Coverage
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SheafComparison

/-!
# The structure sheaf of the big crystalline site

Fix a global crystalline situation `(p, (S, I, γ), X)`.  The structure presheaf of the big
crystalline site sends an object `(U, T, δ)` of `CRIS(X/S)` to the ring `Γ(T, 𝒪_T)` of global
sections of its ambient scheme, and a morphism to the induced map on global sections.  A covering
family of `(U, T, δ)` for the crystalline Zariski topology is a Cartesian family
`{(Uᵢ, Tᵢ, δᵢ) ⟶ (U, T, δ)}` whose family of ambient schemes `{Tᵢ ⟶ T}` is a Zariski covering.
For such a family the sheaf condition asks exactly that a section of `𝒪_T` be determined by, and
be assembled from, compatible sections over the members of an open cover of `T`; so it holds
because `𝒪_T` is a sheaf.  Therefore `(U, T, δ) ↦ Γ(T, 𝒪_T)` is a sheaf of rings `𝒪_{X/S}` on the
big crystalline site.

Being Cartesian is what makes the comparison work: a Cartesian morphism which is an open immersion
on ambient schemes identifies its source with the restriction of its target to the open image, so
a covering family may be replaced by the family of restrictions of `(U, T, δ)` to the opens of `T`
making up the Zariski covering, and the sections of the structure presheaf over those restrictions
are the sections of `𝒪_T` over those opens.

## Main definitions

* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.isoRestrictOpenImage` — the identification of
  the source of a Cartesian open immersion of `CRIS(X/S)` with the restriction of its target to
  the open image of the morphism of ambient schemes.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.coverage` — the Zariski covering families of
  `CRIS(X/S)`, as a coverage.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.crystallineStructureSheaf` — the structure sheaf
  `𝒪_{X/S}` of the big crystalline site, as a sheaf of rings, [Stacks, Tag 07IX].

## Main results

* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.isIso_restrictOpenHom_top` — the restriction
  of an object of `CRIS(X/S)` to the whole of its ambient scheme is that object.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.exists_comp_restrictOpenHom_eq` — the
  universal property of the restriction of an object to an open of its ambient scheme: a morphism
  into that object whose ambient scheme maps into the open factors through the restriction.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.isSheafFor_restrictOpenCover` — a presheaf on
  `CRIS(X/S)` whose restriction to the ambient scheme of an object is a sheaf satisfies the sheaf
  condition for the family of restrictions of that object to an open cover of its ambient scheme.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.isSheafFor_zariskiCovering` — the same
  presheaf satisfies the sheaf condition for every Zariski covering family of that object.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.isSheaf_ringRestriction` — the restriction of
  the structure presheaf of rings to the ambient scheme of an object is a sheaf.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.topology_eq_coverage_toGrothendieck` — the crystalline
  Zariski topology is the topology generated by the coverage of Zariski covering families.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.crisRing_isSheaf` and
  `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.structureSheaf_isSheaf` — the structure presheaf of the
  big crystalline site is a sheaf, as a presheaf of rings and as a presheaf of commutative rings,
  [Stacks, Tag 07IX].

## Implementation notes

The sheaf condition is reduced to Zariski descent on the ambient scheme in two steps.

First, the Zariski covering families form a *coverage*: the pullback condition is witnessed by the
restrictions of the base to the opens over which the members of the family have a factorization,
which is the same family that witnesses cocontinuity of change of base,
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.pullbackLiftHom`.  Hence
`CategoryTheory.Presieve.isSheaf_coverage` reduces the sheaf condition for the generated topology
to the sheaf condition for the Zariski covering families themselves; no base change stability of
those families, [Stacks, Tag 07IA], is needed.

Second, a Zariski covering family is replaced by a family of restrictions to opens.  Each member
is Cartesian and an open immersion on ambient schemes, so
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.isoRestrictOpenImage` identifies it with the
restriction of the base to the open image of its ambient scheme, and
`CategoryTheory.Presieve.isSheafFor_ofArrows_comp_iff` transports the sheaf condition along those
isomorphisms.  For a family of restrictions the sheaf condition is literally the sheaf condition
for the restriction of the presheaf to the ambient scheme, taken for the corresponding open cover,
once the restriction to the whole ambient scheme is identified with the base itself.  For the
structure presheaf that restriction is the structure sheaf of the ambient scheme,
`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.Thickening.restrictionStructureIso`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07IX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07IX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07IB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07IB)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07IQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07IQ)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- **The open immersion of an open which is the whole of a scheme is an isomorphism.** -/
theorem isIso_ι_of_eq_top {X : Scheme.{u}} {V : X.Opens} (hV : V = ⊤) : IsIso V.ι := by
  subst hV
  rw [← Scheme.topIso_hom]
  infer_instance

end AlgebraicGeometry

namespace Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation

namespace Thickening

variable {S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}}

/-- **The restriction of an object of `CRIS(X/S)` to the whole of its ambient scheme is that
object.**  Both components of the structure morphism are the open immersion of a top open. -/
theorem isIso_restrictOpenHom_top (A : Thickening S) :
    IsIso (A.restrictOpenHom (⊤ : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)) := by
  have hs : IsIso (A.restrictOpenHom (⊤ : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)).sourceHom := by
    rw [restrictOpenHom_sourceHom]
    exact isIso_ι_of_eq_top rfl
  have ht : IsIso (A.restrictOpenHom (⊤ : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)).targetHom.hom := by
    rw [restrictOpenHom_targetHom, DividedPowerScheme.restrictι_hom]
    exact isIso_ι_of_eq_top rfl
  exact isIso_of_isIso_sourceHom_targetHom _

/-- **The universal property of the restriction of an object of `CRIS(X/S)` to an open `V` of its
ambient scheme:** a morphism into that object whose ambient scheme maps into `V` factors through
the restriction.  The factorization is the one through the Cartesian open immersion
`A|_V ⟶ A`, which is defined over the open of the source where it exists, here the whole ambient
scheme. -/
theorem exists_comp_restrictOpenHom_eq {A B : Thickening S}
    (V : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens) (r : B ⟶ A)
    (hr : ∀ x : B.thickening.target.scheme, r.targetHom.hom.base x ∈ V) :
    ∃ p : B ⟶ A.restrictOpen V, p ≫ A.restrictOpenHom V = r := by
  have hP : pullbackOpen (A.restrictOpenHom V) r = ⊤ := by
    rw [eq_top_iff]
    intro x _
    change r.targetHom.hom.base x ∈ Set.range (A.restrictOpenHom V).targetHom.hom.base
    exact ⟨⟨r.targetHom.hom.base x, hr x⟩, rfl⟩
  have hiso : IsIso (B.restrictOpenHom (pullbackOpen (A.restrictOpenHom V) r)) := by
    rw [hP]
    exact B.isIso_restrictOpenHom_top
  refine ⟨inv (B.restrictOpenHom (pullbackOpen (A.restrictOpenHom V) r)) ≫
    pullbackLiftHom (A.restrictOpenHom V) r (A.isCartesian_restrictOpenHom V), ?_⟩
  rw [Category.assoc, pullbackLiftHom_comp, IsIso.inv_hom_id_assoc]

section Image

variable {A B : Thickening S} (g : A ⟶ B) [IsOpenImmersion g.targetHom.hom]

/-- **The source of a Cartesian open immersion of `CRIS(X/S)` is the restriction of its target to
the open image of the morphism of ambient schemes.**  Restricting the source to the whole of its
ambient scheme changes nothing, and over that open the comparison with the restriction of the
target to the image is an isomorphism. -/
noncomputable def isoRestrictOpenImage (hg : IsCartesian g) :
    A ≅ B.restrictOpen (g.targetHom.hom ''ᵁ (⊤ : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)) :=
  have := A.isIso_restrictOpenHom_top
  have := isIso_restrictOpenLE (A := A)
    (g.targetHom.hom.preimage_image_eq (⊤ : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)).ge
    (g.targetHom.hom.preimage_image_eq (⊤ : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens))
  have := isIso_restrictOpenMap g hg (g.targetHom.hom ''ᵁ (⊤ : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens))
    (g.targetHom.hom.image_le_opensRange (⊤ : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens))
  (asIso (A.restrictOpenHom (⊤ : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens))).symm ≪≫
    asIso (A.restrictOpenLE
      (g.targetHom.hom.preimage_image_eq (⊤ : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)).ge) ≪≫
    asIso (restrictOpenMap g (g.targetHom.hom ''ᵁ (⊤ : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)))

/-- **The identification of the source of a Cartesian open immersion of `CRIS(X/S)` with the
restriction of its target is compatible with the two morphisms into that target.** -/
theorem isoRestrictOpenImage_hom_restrictOpenHom (hg : IsCartesian g) :
    (isoRestrictOpenImage g hg).hom ≫
        B.restrictOpenHom (g.targetHom.hom ''ᵁ (⊤ : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)) = g := by
  have := A.isIso_restrictOpenHom_top
  have hcomp : (isoRestrictOpenImage g hg).hom =
      inv (A.restrictOpenHom (⊤ : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)) ≫
        A.restrictOpenLE
            (g.targetHom.hom.preimage_image_eq (⊤ : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)).ge ≫
          restrictOpenMap g (g.targetHom.hom ''ᵁ (⊤ : A.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)) := rfl
  rw [hcomp, Category.assoc, Category.assoc, restrictOpenMap_restrictOpenHom,
    restrictOpenLE_restrictOpenHom_assoc, IsIso.inv_hom_id_assoc]

end Image

section Descent

variable (Q : (Thickening S)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u) (B : Thickening S)

/-- **A presheaf on `CRIS(X/S)` whose restriction to the ambient scheme of an object is a sheaf
satisfies the sheaf condition for the restrictions of that object to an open cover of its ambient
scheme.**  The sections of the presheaf over those restrictions are the sections of the restricted
presheaf over the opens, and the restriction to the whole ambient scheme is the object itself. -/
theorem isSheafFor_restrictOpenCover {ι : Type (u + 1)}
    (V : ι → B.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)
    (hV : ∀ x : B.thickening.target.scheme, ∃ i, x ∈ V i)
    (hQ : Presieve.IsSheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥B.thickening.target.scheme)
      (restriction Q B)) :
    Presieve.IsSheafFor Q (B.restrictOpenCover V).presieve₀ := by
  have := B.isIso_restrictOpenHom_top
  have hgen : Sieve.generate (Presieve.ofArrows V (fun i ↦ homOfLE (le_top (a := V i)))) ∈
      Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥B.thickening.target.scheme ⊤ := by
    intro x _
    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hV x
    exact ⟨V i, homOfLE le_top, Sieve.le_generate _ _ _ (Presieve.ofArrows.mk i), hi⟩
  have hsheaf : Presieve.IsSheafFor (restriction Q B)
      (Presieve.ofArrows V (fun i ↦ homOfLE (le_top (a := V i)))) :=
    (Presieve.isSheafFor_iff_generate _).2 (hQ _ hgen)
  have key : ∀ i : ι, B.restrictOpenHom (V i) ≫
      inv (B.restrictOpenHom (⊤ : B.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)) =
        B.restrictOpenLE (le_top (a := V i)) := fun i ↦ by
    rw [IsIso.comp_inv_eq]
    exact (restrictOpenLE_restrictOpenHom B (le_top (a := V i))).symm
  have hpre : ((B.restrictOpenCover V).presieve₀ : Presieve B) =
      Presieve.ofArrows (fun i ↦ B.restrictOpen (V i))
        (fun i ↦ B.restrictOpenHom (V i)) := rfl
  rw [hpre, Presieve.isSheafFor_arrows_iff]
  intro x hx
  have hx' : Presieve.Arrows.Compatible (restriction Q B)
      (fun i ↦ homOfLE (le_top (a := V i))) x := by
    intro i j W gi gj _
    exact hx i j (B.restrictOpen W) (B.restrictOpenLE (leOfHom gi))
      (B.restrictOpenLE (leOfHom gj))
      (show B.restrictOpenLE (leOfHom gi) ≫ B.restrictOpenHom (V i) =
          B.restrictOpenLE (leOfHom gj) ≫ B.restrictOpenHom (V j) by
        rw [restrictOpenLE_restrictOpenHom, restrictOpenLE_restrictOpenHom])
  obtain ⟨t, ht, htuniq⟩ :
      ∃! t : Q.obj (op (B.restrictOpen (⊤ : B.thickening.target.scheme.Opens))),
        ∀ i : ι, Q.map (B.restrictOpenLE (le_top (a := V i))).op t = x i :=
    (Presieve.isSheafFor_arrows_iff _ _).1 hsheaf x hx'
  refine ⟨Q.map (inv (B.restrictOpenHom (⊤ : B.thickening.target.scheme.Opens))).op t,
    fun i ↦ ?_, fun s hs ↦ ?_⟩
  · rw [← Functor.map_comp_apply, ← op_comp, key i]
    exact ht i
  · have h1 : ∀ i : ι, Q.map (B.restrictOpenLE (le_top (a := V i))).op
        (Q.map (B.restrictOpenHom (⊤ : B.thickening.target.scheme.Opens)).op s) = x i := by
      intro i
      rw [← Functor.map_comp_apply, ← op_comp, restrictOpenLE_restrictOpenHom]
      exact hs i
    rw [← htuniq _ h1, ← Functor.map_comp_apply, ← op_comp, IsIso.inv_hom_id, op_id,
      Functor.map_id_apply]

/-- **A presheaf on `CRIS(X/S)` whose restriction to the ambient scheme of an object is a sheaf
satisfies the sheaf condition for every Zariski covering family of that object.**  Each member of
the family is Cartesian and an open immersion on ambient schemes, hence identified with the
restriction of the object to the open image of its ambient scheme, and the family of those open
images covers the ambient scheme. -/
theorem isSheafFor_zariskiCovering (E : PreZeroHypercover.{u + 1} B) (hE : IsZariskiCovering E)
    (hQ : Presieve.IsSheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥B.thickening.target.scheme)
      (restriction Q B)) :
    Presieve.IsSheafFor Q E.presieve₀ := by
  have hE' : (∀ x, ∃ i, x ∈ Set.range ((E.f i).targetHom.hom).base) ∧
      ∀ i, IsOpenImmersion (E.f i).targetHom.hom := by
    simpa [targetPresieve] using hE.2
  have := hE'.2
  have hfun : E.f = fun i ↦ (isoRestrictOpenImage (E.f i) (hE.1 i)).hom ≫
      B.restrictOpenHom ((E.f i).targetHom.hom ''ᵁ
        (⊤ : (E.X i).thickening.target.scheme.Opens)) :=
    funext fun i ↦ (isoRestrictOpenImage_hom_restrictOpenHom (E.f i) (hE.1 i)).symm
  have hcov : ∀ x : B.thickening.target.scheme, ∃ i,
      x ∈ (E.f i).targetHom.hom ''ᵁ (⊤ : (E.X i).thickening.target.scheme.Opens) := fun x ↦ by
    obtain ⟨i, y, hy⟩ := hE'.1 x
    exact ⟨i, y, trivial, hy⟩
  rw [show (E.presieve₀ : Presieve B) = _ from
    congrArg (Presieve.ofArrows (fun i ↦ E.X i)) hfun]
  exact (Presieve.isSheafFor_ofArrows_comp_iff
      (fun i ↦ B.restrictOpenHom ((E.f i).targetHom.hom ''ᵁ
        (⊤ : (E.X i).thickening.target.scheme.Opens)))
      (fun i ↦ isoRestrictOpenImage (E.f i) (hE.1 i))).2
    (isSheafFor_restrictOpenCover Q B
      (fun i ↦ (E.f i).targetHom.hom ''ᵁ (⊤ : (E.X i).thickening.target.scheme.Opens)) hcov hQ)

end Descent

/-- **The restriction of the structure presheaf of rings of the big crystalline site to the
ambient scheme of an object is a sheaf.**  It is the structure sheaf of that scheme, read as a
sheaf of rings. -/
theorem isSheaf_ringRestriction (B : Thickening S) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥B.thickening.target.scheme)
      (ringRestriction B) :=
  (Presheaf.isSheaf_of_iso_iff (Functor.isoWhiskerRight (restrictionStructureIso B)
      (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u}))).2
    (Presheaf.isSheaf_comp_of_isSheaf _ _ (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})
      B.thickening.target.scheme.IsSheaf)

end Thickening

open Thickening

/-- **The Zariski covering families of `CRIS(X/S)`, as a coverage.**  A Zariski covering family of
`B` pulled back along a morphism `p : A ⟶ B` is refined by the restrictions of `A` to the opens of
its ambient scheme over which `p` factors through the members of the family. -/
def coverage (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) : Coverage (Thickening S) where
  toPrecoverage := precoverage S
  pullback := by
    rintro B A p R ⟨E, rfl, hE⟩
    have hE' : (∀ x, ∃ i, x ∈ Set.range ((E.f i).targetHom.hom).base) ∧
        ∀ i, IsOpenImmersion (E.f i).targetHom.hom := by
      simpa [targetPresieve] using hE.2
    refine ⟨(A.restrictOpenCover (fun i ↦ have := hE'.2 i; pullbackOpen (E.f i) p)).presieve₀,
      ⟨_, rfl, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
    · refine isZariskiCovering_restrictOpenCover _ _ fun x ↦ ?_
      obtain ⟨i, y, hy⟩ := hE'.1 (p.targetHom.hom.base x)
      exact ⟨i, y, hy⟩
    · rintro Z m ⟨i⟩
      have := hE'.2 i
      exact ⟨E.X i, pullbackLiftHom (E.f i) p (hE.1 i), E.f i, ⟨i⟩,
        pullbackLiftHom_comp (E.f i) p (hE.1 i)⟩

/-- **The crystalline Zariski topology is the topology generated by the coverage of Zariski
covering families.** -/
theorem topology_eq_coverage_toGrothendieck (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) :
    topology S = (coverage S).toGrothendieck := by
  change (coverage S).toPrecoverage.toGrothendieck = (coverage S).toGrothendieck
  exact Coverage.toGrothendieck_toPrecoverage (coverage S)

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 07IX.**  The structure presheaf of rings of the big crystalline site is
a sheaf for the crystalline Zariski topology.  It suffices to check the Zariski covering families,
and for such a family the condition is Zariski descent for the structure sheaf of the ambient
scheme of the base. -/
@[stacks 07IX "the structure presheaf is a sheaf of rings"]
theorem crisRing_isSheaf (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf (topology S) (crisRing S) := by
  intro R₀
  rw [topology_eq_coverage_toGrothendieck, Presieve.isSheaf_coverage]
  rintro B R ⟨E, rfl, hE⟩
  exact isSheafFor_zariskiCovering _ B E hE (isSheaf_ringRestriction B R₀)

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 07IX.**  The structure presheaf of commutative rings of the big
crystalline site is a sheaf for the crystalline Zariski topology. -/
@[stacks 07IX "the structure presheaf is a sheaf of commutative rings"]
theorem structureSheaf_isSheaf (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf (topology S) (structureSheaf S) :=
  Presheaf.isSheaf_of_isSheaf_comp _ _ (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})
    (crisRing_isSheaf S)

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 07IX.**  The structure sheaf `𝒪_{X/S}` of the big crystalline site: the
sheaf of rings on `CRIS(X/S)` sending an object `(U, T, δ)` to the ring `Γ(T, 𝒪_T)` of global
sections of its ambient scheme. -/
@[stacks 07IX "the structure sheaf"]
def crystallineStructureSheaf (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u}) :
    Sheaf (topology S) RingCat.{u} :=
  ⟨crisRing S, crisRing_isSheaf S⟩

end Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation

end
